                    <h2 id="seller-tickets-POSTapi-v1-seller-tickets--id--reply">Reply to a ticket</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Adds a seller reply to the ticket conversation.
Optionally, the seller can add an internal note visible only to staff.
Cannot reply to closed or escalated tickets.</p>

<span id="example-requests-POSTapi-v1-seller-tickets--id--reply">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request POST \
    "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/seller/tickets/1/reply" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_API_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"message\": \"I have resent the activation key to your email.\",
    \"is_internal_note\": false
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/seller/tickets/1/reply"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_API_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "message": "I have resent the activation key to your email.",
    "is_internal_note": false
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "POST",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

